{
    "background_story": "Zainab was a talented artist known for her vivid paintings, but also for her constant complaining. She would often grumble about the smallest things, from the quality of the paint to the noise level in her studio. Her friends and family had grown accustomed to her complainingly nature, but it sometimes made them want to pull their hair out. One day, while working on a new piece, Zainab's complaints reached new heights. She grumbled about the weather, the music, and even the coffee she was drinking. Just as she was about to give up, a wise old artist walked into her studio and told her, 'Your complaining is like a stormy weather, it will pass, but the art you create will remain.' Zainab took his words to heart and learned to channel her energy into her art, creating some of her most breathtaking pieces yet.",
